   "text": {
    "L1": "Gauri did not come home, so her friends became worried.",
    "L2": "They went to look for her and searched near the mango grove.",
    "L3": "Then Meena heard a tinkle from Gauri's bell.",
    "L4": "The friends followed the sound and found Gauri in thorny bushes.",
    "L5": "They freed her and brought her home, feeling happy.",
    "L6": "A good retelling keeps the events in order: first, next, then, and at last.",
    "L7": "Past words are not always made by adding -ed: we say went, found, and ran.",
    "L8": "Now put the story events in order."
   },
